14:03:24.879 > l
14:03:24.936 | Passing the Aureliana Forest. (road)
14:03:24.942 | Nature's fecundity floods the surrounds with the clamour of life in a chittering refrain. Vines have overtaken this location. This area is unnaturally flooded with water. Dawn rises upon a cloudless sky, the dim, reddish rays of the sun shining down upon the land. All along the southern perimeter of this stretch of highway lies the Aureliana Forest. Its presence soothes the eyes with muted greens and browns, the scents of pine and cedar tantalise your nostrils. An urge to postpone your journey and see what wonders might be discovered within its depths crosses your thoughts, but soon vanishes as softly as it appeared. Sometimes you think that perhaps there is a silent war raging here, between forest and grassland, with only the Gods aware of the final outcome. A large cart rests here, stacked high with assorted containers secured with thick rope. The opaque form of a phantom harp seal drifts here. A daemonic hyena awaits in savage readiness, her cold eyes burning with cunning malevolence amidst the steady exhalation of crimson fog from slavering jaws. Valkyri, Seeker of Elocution is here. She wields a flail in each hand. The soul of Belaziel roams the land, bodiless. Na'vroth Pharaus Lichlord is riding on a phantom harp seal. His features are obscured by a mask of lifevision beneath the raised hood of a Hood of the Sphinx. He wields a daemon-forged scimitar bound in dark chains in his left hand and a chain-wreathed scimitar with a daemonic guard in his right. The Red Dragon Zaphael's imposing form looms.
