14:03:41.955 | Nature's fecundity floods the surrounds with the clamour of life in a chittering refrain. Vines have overtaken this location. This area is unnaturally flooded with water. Dawn rises upon a cloudless sky, the dim, reddish rays of the sun shining down upon the land. Just to the south of the highway lies the large, fresh-water lake known as Vundamere. The highway verge is trampled and an obvious path cuts through the grasses to the lake shore, indicating its popularity as a resting place. The water shimmers blue and inviting, perhaps a stroll along the shore would not be out of place. North of the highway is one of the most curious artefacts ever discovered in Achaea, an ivy-covered archway, standing as a gateway to places and things found nowhere else in the land. If you pause here long enough you might see the comings and goings of many Achaeans, mostly young, eager and excited about the adventures they will find here. Although busy, it is also strangely peaceful. A small wooden sign is nailed crookedly to a post here. A little girl in a mermaid costume stands here, looking around eagerly. The opaque form of a phantom harp seal drifts here. A daemonic hyena awaits in savage readiness, her cold eyes burning with cunning malevolence amidst the steady exhalation of crimson fog from slavering jaws. A phantom spider lurks in the shadows, the outline of its hulking frame scarcely discernible. Hands of rotting flesh and white bone push up from the ground. Tyndran Tabethys Aristata, Tyrannical Butcher of Baelgrim is riding on a hulking phantom spider. She wields an exquisite Mhaldorian staff of sterling silver in her left hand and a Shield of Absorption in her right. Steward Layta Lichlord, Red Reaper is here, hidden. Her features are obscured by an unsettling porcelain doll-face mask. She wields Agith'maal's ire in her left hand and a bone shield reinforced with blackened steel in her right. Warden Sinit d'Ivoire is here. Na'vroth Pharaus Lichlord is riding on a phantom harp seal. His features are obscured by a mask of lifevision beneath the raised hood of a Hood of the Sphinx. He wields a daemon-forged scimitar bound in dark chains in his left hand and a chain-wreathed scimitar with a daemonic guard in his right.
